          },
          "title": "<br>COURS (HIVER) / COURSES (WINTER)",
          "text": "<p>Make your own website in a few clicks! Mobirise helps you cut down development time by providing you with a flexible website editor with a drag and drop interface. MobiRise Website Builder creates responsive, retina and mobile friendly websites in a few clicks. Mobirise is one of the easiest website development tools available today. It also gives you the freedom to develop as many websites as you like given the fact that it is a desktop app.</p>",
          "button": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" class=\"mbr-buttons__btn btn btn-lg btn-default\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\">LEARN MORE</a>",
          "_tags": [
            "Thème"
          ],
          "meta": "By John Smith posted July 30, 2015",
          "_name": "content5",
          "_anchor": "content5-2z",
          "_sourceTheme": "default"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "showMeta": true
          },
          "title": "CHM3331 - Chimie bio-organique : De molécule à nanomachine",
          "meta": "Cours de premier cycle en chimie - Faculté des arts et des sciences, U. de Montréal Undergraduate chemistry course - Arts and Science Faculty, U. of Montreal",
          "_tags": [
            "Thème"
          ],
          "_name": "header3",
          "_styles": {
            "H3": {
              "font-size": "20px"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "header3-2w",
          "_sourceTheme": "default"
        },
        {
          "text": "<p>\n</p><div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Concepts tirés de la nature qui transforment la chimie, dont: l'auto-assemblage, les interrupteurs moléculaires, la biocatalyse, la sélection de librairies moléculaires, la chimie médicinale, la nanotechnologie et la biologie synthétique.</div><div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Concepts derived from nature that transform chemistry, including: self-assembly, molecular switches, biocatalysis, molecular library selection, medicinal chemistry, nanotechnology and synthetic biology.\n</div>",
          "_tags": [
            "Thème"
          ],
          "_name": "content1",
          "_params": {},
          "_anchor": "content1-2x",
          "_sourceTheme": "default"
        },
        {
          "buttons": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" class=\"mbr-buttons__btn btn btn-lg btn-danger\" href=\"https://admission.umontreal.ca/cours-et-horaires/cours/chm-3331/\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\" target=\"_blank\">DETAILS</a> ",
          "_tags": [
            "Thème"
          ],
          "_name": "buttons1",
          "_params": {},
          "_anchor": "buttons1-2y",
          "_sourceTheme": "default"
        },
        {
          "_params": {
            "paddingTop": 3,
            "paddingBottom": 3,
            "bgImageRadio": false,
            "bgImage": "images/bg3.jpg",
            "parallax": true,
            "bgColorRadio": true,
            "bgColor": "#3c3c3c",
            "overlay": true,
            "overlayColor": "#3C3C3C",
            "overlayOpacity": 0.8,
            "googleMap": {
              "address": "MIL campus",
              "state": "ok",
              "stateDetails": ""
            }
          },
          "text1": "<strong>ADRESSE / ADDRESS</strong><br><br>Université de Montréal \n<br>Département de Chimie<br><a href=\"https://campusmil.umontreal.ca/\" class=\"text-warning text-primary\" target=\"_blank\">Campus MIL</a> - Local B-6227&nbsp;<br>1375 Ave.Thérèse-Lavoie-Roux<br>Montreal, Qc, Canada,&nbsp;H2V 0B3&nbsp;<br>\n<br><b>CONTACT</b><br>Phone: +1 <a href=\"tel:+1 (514) 343-2124 \" class=\"text-warning\">(514) 343-2124 </a>\n<br>Fax: +1 <a href=\"tel:+1 (514) 343-7586 \" class=\"text-warning\">(514) 343-7586 </a>\n<br>@ :<a href=\"mailto:joelle.pelletier@umontreal.ca\" class=\"text-warning\"> joelle.pelletier@umontreal.ca&nbsp;</a><br><br>",
          "text2": "<p class=\"mbr-contacts__text\"><b>LIENS / LINKS</b></p><p class=\"mbr-contacts__text\"><b><br></b></p><p class=\"mbr-contacts__text\"><b><a href=\"http://www.proteo.ca/en/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"text-warning\">PROTEO</a></b></p><p class=\"mbr-contacts__text\"><u><a href=\"https://chimie.umontreal.ca/repertoire-departement/professeurs/professeur/in/in14450/sg/Joelle%20Pelletier/\" class=\"text-gray\" target=\"_blank\">Joelle Pelletier - Chemistry Dpt.</a></u><br></p><p class=\"mbr-contacts__text\"><u><a href=\"http://ccvc.research.mcgill.ca/home.html\" class=\"text-warning\">Centre in Green Chemistry and Catalysis (<b>CGCC</b>)</a></u></p><p class=\"mbr-contacts__text\"><u><a href=\"https://www.affiniteinstruments.com/\" class=\"text-gray\" target=\"_blank\">Affinity Instruments</a></u></p>",
          "_tags": [
            "Theme"
          ],
          "_name": "contacts2",
          "_styles": {
            "DIV": {
              "color": "#ffffff"
            }
          },
          "_anchor": "contacts2-5b",
